From: Abue Ammar <14371506+abue-ammar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:54:28 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Clear the running dot as soon as an app quits (#1678)

RunningAppsMonitor re-read NSWorkspace.runningApplications on
didTerminateApplicationNotification, but that notification arrives while
the list still holds the quitting app. The refresh saw no change, so the
dot and the running-only actions stayed until some later launch or quit.

Observe runningApplications with KVO instead. It fires in the same pass,
once the list has changed; .initial replaces the startup refresh, and the
observation invalidates itself on deinit.
---
 .../Launcher/Service/RunningAppsMonitor.swift    | 16 +++++-----------
 docs/features/launcher.md                        |  6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Tinycast/Features/Launcher/Service/RunningAppsMonitor.swift b/Tinycast/Features/Launcher/Service/RunningAppsMonitor.swift
index b249a53a..d615245a 100644
--- a/Tinycast/Features/Launcher/Service/RunningAppsMonitor.swift
+++ b/Tinycast/Features/Launcher/Service/RunningAppsMonitor.swift
@@ -5,19 +5,13 @@ import AppKit
 final class RunningAppsMonitor {
     private(set) var runningBundleIDs: Set<String> = []
     private var runningAppPaths: Set<String> = []
-    @ObservationIgnored private var observers: [NotificationToken] = []
+    @ObservationIgnored private var observation: NSKeyValueObservation?
 
     init() {
-        refresh()
-        let center = NSWorkspace.shared.notificationCenter
-        for name in [
-            NSWorkspace.didLaunchApplicationNotification,
-            NSWorkspace.didTerminateApplicationNotification
-        ] {
-            let token = center.addObserver(forName: name, object: nil, queue: .main) { [weak self] _ in
-                MainActor.assumeIsolated { self?.refresh() }
-            }
-            observers.append(NotificationToken(token, center: center))
+        observation = NSWorkspace.shared.observe(
+            \.runningApplications, options: .initial
+        ) { [weak self] _, _ in
+            MainActor.assumeIsolated { self?.refresh() }
         }
     }
 
diff --git a/docs/features/launcher.md b/docs/features/launcher.md
index 234a3b10..b808bfac 100644
--- a/docs/features/launcher.md
+++ b/docs/features/launcher.md
@@ -825,8 +825,10 @@ not drag.
 
 ## Quitting and restarting apps
 
-`RunningAppsMonitor` (live from `NSWorkspace` launch/terminate notifications) drives both the row's
-running dot and the availability of the running-only actions:
+`RunningAppsMonitor` (live from a KVO observation of `NSWorkspace.runningApplications`) drives both the
+row's running dot and the availability of the running-only actions. It observes the list rather than
+`didTerminateApplicationNotification`, which arrives while the list still holds the quitting app, so
+reading the list there left the dot on until some later launch or quit:
 
 - **Quit Application** — a row of an app's ⌘K Actions menu, shown only while that app is
   running, also bound to **⌃⇧Q** on the selected row. The chord guard mirrors the menu row's
